! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F202A sub-tests 15-20
! (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf p.33, octal 011400.00-011432.40) --
! a real FP-compare block of the diagnostic RUN on this model.
!
! Each sub-test loads an operand (unnormalized), zeroes the indicators,
! COMPARES it (K, unnormalized) against a constant, and checks the
! arithmetic comparison indicators AL/AE/AH with three SIC-prefixed
! branch-on-indicator instructions that go to the error routine SERS if
! the result is wrong. The listing's own comment states the expected
! result. Two directions are exercised:
!   A15-A18: load FPK21, compare FPK27 / FPK1 / FK34 / FK40 -- expect
!            AH on (FPK21 is arithmetically greater). Checks BZAH (error
!            if AH off), BAL (error if AL on), BAE (error if AE on),
!            across the XFN / N / XFP operand ranges.
!   A19-A20: load FPK2, compare FPK26 / FPK21 -- expect AL on (FPK2 is
!            arithmetically less). Checks BZAL, BAE, BAH.
! A correct FP compare falls straight through all six sub-tests to
! F202A21's location, where this transcription substitutes a PASS halt
! (BEW,$); any wrong indicator branches to SERS, where a FAIL halt sits.
! PC alone says pass (halted at PASS) or fail (halted at SERS) -- the
! self-checking mechanism the I-Box SIC-CB block uses.
!
! Substitutions (the SSIP diagnostic framework, all OUTSIDE the
! transcribed code range, at their real listed low-memory addresses so
! the SIC/branch machine code still matches the listing):
!   SERS (octal 1304) -> BEW,$   the error routine, replaced by a halt
!   SEN  (octal 1310) -> a scratch word the SIC stores the IC into
!   PASS (octal 11433, where F202A21 begins) -> BEW,$
! The seven FP constants come from the pools on p.176-178 at their
! listed addresses, as the raw 64-bit floating-point words %8=DD%BU=
! defines.
!
! Instructions used: L(U), Z, K(U), SIC, BZAL/BZAH/BAL/BAE/BAH (branch
! on indicator), BEW -- all implemented. This verifies the single-
! precision FP compare against the diagnostic's own operands, both the
! AL and AH outcomes, over three exponent ranges. The SIC pairs are
! full words at octal .40, exercising the half-word-aligned full-word
! placement fixed this session (strap/README.md Gotchas item 19).
! verify_fp_compare_listing.py checks every transcribed half-word and
! every constant against the printed machine code.
!
! Observed: the model halts at PASS -- every compare sets exactly the
! indicator IBM's diagnostic expects (AH for A15-A18, AL for A19-A20).
! Injection (AL and AH swapped in StretchExecute's FP compare arm): the
! model halts at SERS (the FAIL routine) at the first sub-test, exactly
! as predicted. Reversed by the exact inverse edit (AGENTS.md rule 2).

! -- SSIP framework substitutes, at their real listed addresses --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $              ! error routine -> FAIL halt
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0      ! SIC stores the instruction counter here

! -- floating-point constants (pools, p.176-178) --
        SLC, (8)22006.0
FPK1    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777777777777777777777
FPK2    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777777777777777777760
        SLC, (8)22032.0
FPK21   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031177777777777777767
        SLC, (8)22037.0
FPK26   DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777577777777777777760
FPK27   DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777677777777777777760
        SLC, (8)22204.0
FK34    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0200377777777777777770
        SLC, (8)22212.0
FK40    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777577777777777777770

! -- the transcribed code (verbatim, at the listing's own addresses) --
        SLC, (8)11400.0
F202A15 L(U), FPK21         ! N RNG G  FRACT +   AH ON
        Z, $IND
        K(U), FPK27         ! XFN RANGE, FRACT.+
        SIC, SEN
        BZAH, SERS          ! error if AH off and AL or AE on
        SIC, SEN
        BAL, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAE, SERS
F202A16 L(U), FPK21
        Z, $IND
        K(U), FPK1          ! XFN RANGE, FRACT.-
        SIC, SEN
        BZAH, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAL, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAE, SERS
F202A17 L(U), FPK21
        Z, $IND
        K(U), FK34          ! N RANGE, FRACT.-
        SIC, SEN
        BZAH, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAL, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAE, SERS
F202A18 L(U), FPK21
        Z, $IND
        K(U), FK40          ! XFP RANGE, FRACT.-
        SIC, SEN
        BZAH, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAL, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAE, SERS
F202A19 L(U), FPK2          ! XFN RNG  FRACT +   AL ON
        Z, $IND
        K(U), FPK26         ! XFP RANGE, FRACT.+
        SIC, SEN
        BZAL, SERS          ! error if AL off and AE or AH on
        SIC, SEN
        BAE, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAH, SERS
F202A20 L(U), FPK2
        Z, $IND
        K(U), FPK21         ! N RANGE, FRACT.+
        SIC, SEN
        BZAL, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAE, SERS
        SIC, SEN
        BAH, SERS

! -- PASS halt where F202A21 begins --
        SLC, (8)11433.0
PASS    BEW, $              ! all checks fell through: success

        END, F202A15
